**Definition 5.1 (Normalized event multipliers and all TP multipliers).**
For the fifteen residuals (1.11) choose real positive semidefinite
$A_J^\pm$ with
$\sum_J\operatorname{tr}(A_J^++A_J^-)=1$. Define

$$
\begin{gathered}
Z_J=A_J^+-A_J^-,\qquad
\beta=\sum_J\operatorname{tr}(Z_J\Pi_J),\qquad
h(E)=(\operatorname{tr}(H_iE))_i,\\
C=\sum_Jt_Jh(Z_J)^T,\qquad
\delta_\nu=\sum_J\operatorname{tr}(Z_JP_\nu(\Pi_J)),\qquad
y\in\mathbb R^3.
\end{gathered}
\tag{5.1}
$$

These are precisely the data in
[QJM, Convention 6.3](RECURSIVE_RELATIONAL_OBSERVATION_QUANTUM_JOINT_MARGINAL_AND_ATTAINING_PORT.md),
with $\delta_\nu$ denoting its $d_\nu$. Matrix (3.1) is its
$B_y(a)$. The same $C,\delta,y$ must be used in every population,
atom and event calculation; they are not chosen separately on
different faces. Real multipliers suffice for these real event
matrices: replacing a Hermitian PSD multiplier by its entrywise
real part preserves PSD on real vectors and every trace pairing
with real symmetric matrices, as well as its trace.

